-- src:6410 | withdrawn;
-- src:6412 | (d) an application for any direction or order mentioned in section 58(1).
@ref Seventh Schedule para 3(1) (src:6394-6412)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 7 matter before the court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(1) the matter is one of cases (a) to (d), for a single Judge or 2 Judges of the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `sch 7 an application to record a judgment or order made by consent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 7 an application for an order incidental to a judgment or order made by consent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 7 an application to adduce further evidence in proceedings before the court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 7 an application for costs, or any other matter remaining to be dealt with, after an application or appeal is withdrawn` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 7 an application for a direction or order mentioned in section 40(1) or 58(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following cases may be heard and decided by the Court of Appeal consisting of a single Judge or 2 Judges" [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

