-- src:6420 | (b) the power under section 29E(1) to transfer to the Appellate Division an
-- src:6421 | appeal that has been made to the Court of Appeal.
@ref Seventh Schedule para 3(2) (src:6414-6421)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 7 matter before the court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 para 3(2) the matter is one of the two transfer powers a single Judge or 2 Judges of the Court of Appeal may exercise` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `sch 7 the power under section 29D(1) to transfer to the Court of Appeal an appeal made to the Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 7 the power under section 29E(1) to transfer to the Appellate Division an appeal made to the Court of Appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court of Appeal consisting of a single Judge or 2 Judges may exercise the following powers" [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

